    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33823" root="فست and فستط" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُسْتَاطٌ</span></b> , also written <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِسْتَاطٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُسْطَاطٌ</span>, in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فسط</span>, to which it belongs; for the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ت</span> is a substitute for the [former] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ط</span> in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فسطاط</span>, or for the
[latter] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">س</span> in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِسَّاطٌ</span>. (M and TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فسط</span>.)

